Export the per-node score vector that run.py already computes.

run.py builds `ano_score_final` -- the mean anomaly score per node over
`--auc_test_rounds` rounds -- measures an AUC on it, prints the AUC and then
uses the vector only for a degree-split breakdown it also prints. GraFlag
publishes the scores a method computed rather than a number it printed, so the
vector has to leave the process.

Written behind an environment variable so the patched file behaves exactly as
upstream when GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT is unset -- running the repository's own
commands from its README produces byte-identical output to the unpatched tree.

The labels are written beside the scores because run.py's `ano_label` comes
from its own `load_mat`, and pairing the published scores with a label column
read separately would depend on both agreeing about node order.

Generated with `git diff` against the tree SOURCE_REF pins.

diff --git a/AD-GCL/run.py b/AD-GCL/run.py
index 30eabee..d9cac13 100644
--- a/AD-GCL/run.py
+++ b/AD-GCL/run.py
@@ -318,6 +318,10 @@ auc = roc_auc_score(ano_label, ano_score_final)
 
 print('AUC:{:.4f}'.format(auc))
 
+if os.environ.get('GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'):
+    np.savetxt(os.environ['GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'], ano_score_final)
+    np.savetxt(os.environ['GRAFLAG_SCORE_OUT'] + '.label', ano_label)
+
 out_degrees = dgl_graph.out_degrees().numpy()
 
 result = np.column_stack((ano_label, ano_score_final, out_degrees))
